16:10 And when you announce all these words to this people , they will say to you : ‘Why would the Lord pronounce all this great evil against us ?
And they abandoned me , and they did not keep my law .
For behold , each one walks after the depravity of his own evil heart , so that he does not listen to me .
And in that place , you will serve , day and night , strange gods who will not give you rest .
16:15 but instead , ‘As the Lord lives , who led the sons of Israel away from the land of the north , ’ and from all the lands to which I have cast them out .
16:18 But first , I will repay their double iniquities and their sins .
And they will know that the Lord is my name.”
17:1 “The sin of Judah has been written with a pen of iron and a point of diamond .
17:2 And their sons make a remembrance of their shrines , and their sacred groves , and their leafy trees on high mountains ,
And I will cause you to serve your enemies in a land that you do not know .
17:5 Thus says the Lord : “Cursed is a man who trusts in man , and who establishes what is flesh as his right arm , and whose heart withdraws from the Lord .
17:7 Blessed is the man who trusts in the Lord , for the Lord will be his confidence .
And it will not fear when the heat arrives .
And in the time of drought , it will not be anxious , nor will it cease at any time to bear fruit .
17:10 I am the Lord , who examines the heart and tests the temperament , who gives to each one according to his way and according to the fruit of his own decisions .
In the midst of his days , he will leave it all behind , and he will be foolish concerning his very end.”
For they have abandoned the Lord , the Source of living waters .
That which has gone forth from my lips has been right in your sight .
You are my hope in the day of affliction .
May they be fearful , and may I not be fearful .
17:19 Thus says the Lord to me : “Go , and stand at the gate of the sons of the people , through which the kings of Judah enter and depart , and at all the gates of Jerusalem .
17:21 Thus says the Lord : “Guard your souls , and do not choose to carry heavy things on the day of the Sabbath , nor should you carry these things through the gates of Jerusalem .
Sanctify the day of the Sabbath , just as I instructed your fathers .
Instead , they hardened their neck , lest they listen to me and receive discipline .
17:25 then there will enter through the gates of this city : kings and princes , sitting on the throne of David , and riding on chariots and horses , they and their princes , the men of Judah and the inhabitants of Jerusalem .
17:26 And they will arrive from the cities of Judah and from all around Jerusalem , and from the land of Benjamin , and from the plains , and from the mountainous regions , and from the south , carrying holocausts , and victims , and sacrifices , and frankincense .
17:27 But if you will not listen to me , to sanctify the day of the Sabbath , and not to carry burdens , and not to bring these things through the gates of Jerusalem on the day of the Sabbath , then I will kindle a fire at its gates , and it will devour the houses of Jerusalem , and it will not be extinguished.”
18:1 The word that came to Jeremiah from the Lord , saying :
18:3 And I descended into the house of the potter , and behold , he was making a work on the wheel .
And turning away , he made another vessel , for it had been pleasing in his eyes to make it .
18:7 Suddenly , I will speak against a nation and against a kingdom , so that I may uproot , and destroy , and scatter it .
18:9 And soon , I will speak about a nation and about a kingdom , so that I may build and plant it .
18:11 Now , therefore , speak to the men of Judah and to the inhabitants of Jerusalem , saying : Thus says the Lord : Behold , I am forming an evil against you , and I am considering a plan against you .
18:15 Yet my people have forgotten me , offering useless libations , and stumbling in their ways , in the paths of the world , so that they walk by these on an unmarked route .
Each one who passes by will be astonished and will shake his head .
I will show them the back , and not the face , in the day of their perdition.”
For the law will not perish from the priest , nor counsel from the wise , nor a sermon from the prophet .
For they have dug a pit for my soul !
18:21 Because of this , give their sons over to famine , and bring them to the hand of the sword .
And let their husbands be slain by death .
19:2 And go out to the valley of the son of Hinnom , which is near the entrance to the earthen gate , and there you shall proclaim the words that I will speak to you .
Thus says the Lord of hosts , the God of Israel : Behold , I will lead an affliction over this place , so much so that it will ring in the ears of all who hear about it .
And they have filled this place with the blood of the innocent .
19:6 Because of this , behold , the days are approaching , says the Lord , when this place will no longer be called Topheth , or the valley of the son of Hinnom , but the Valley of Slaughter .
And I will overthrow them with the sword , in the sight of their enemies and by the hand of those who seek their lives .
19:8 And I will set this city amid stupor and hissing .
19:9 And I will feed them with the flesh of their sons and with the flesh of their daughters .
And they will be buried at Topheth , because there will be no other place for burial .
And I will make this city to be like Topheth .
19:14 Then Jeremiah arrived from Topheth , where the Lord had sent him to prophesy , and he stood in the atrium of the house of the Lord , and he said to all the people :
For they have hardened their necks , so that they would not heed my words.”
20:1 And Pashhur , the son of Immer , the priest who had been appointed leader in the house of the Lord , heard Jeremiah prophesying these words .
20:3 And when it had become light on the next day , Pashhur led Jeremiah from the stocks .
20:4 For thus says the Lord : “Behold , I will give you over to fear , you and all your friends , and they will fall by the sword of their enemies , and your eyes will see it .
And he will lead them away to Babylon , and he will strike them with the sword .
And I will give all the treasures of the kings of Judah into the hands of their enemies .
20:6 But you , Pashhur , and all the inhabitants of your house , will go into captivity .
And there you shall die .
I have become a derision all day long ; everyone mocks me .
And the word of the Lord has been made into a reproach against me and a derision , all day long .
And my heart became like a raging fire , enclosed within my bones .
‘If only there were some way that he might be deceived , and we might prevail against him and obtain vengeance from him !
For this reason , those who persecute me will fall , and they will be ineffective .
For they have not understood the everlasting disgrace that will never be wiped away .
For I have revealed my case to you .
Praise the Lord !
20:15 Cursed is the man who announced it to my father , saying , ‘A male child has been born to you , ’ causing him to rejoice with gladness .
Let him hear an outcry in the morning , and wailing at the time of midday !
20:18 Why did I depart from the womb , so that I would see hardship and sorrow , and so that my days would be consumed by trouble ?
21:1 The word that came to Jeremiah from the Lord , when king Zedekiah sent Pashhur , the son of Malchiah , and Zephaniah , the son of Maaseiah , the priest , to him , saying :
Perhaps it may be that the Lord will act toward us according to all his wonders , and he may withdraw from us.”
21:4 Thus says the Lord , the God of Israel : Behold , I will turn back the weapons of war that are in your hands , with which you fight against the king of Babylon and the Chaldeans , who besiege you at the surrounding walls .
21:5 And I myself will make war against you : with an outstretched hand , and with a strong arm , and in fury , and in indignation , and in great wrath .
21:7 And afterward , thus says the Lord : I will give Zedekiah , the king of Judah , and his servants , and his people , and those who have been left behind in this city after pestilence and the sword and famine , into the hand of Nebuchadnezzar , the king of Babylon , and into the hand of their enemies , and into the hand of those who seek their lives .
21:9 Whoever lives in this city will die by the sword , and by famine , and by pestilence .
21:13 Behold , I am against you , O inhabitants of a valley with firm and level ground , says the Lord .
And who can enter into our houses ? ’
And I will kindle a fire in its forest .
22:2 And you shall say : Listen to the word of the Lord , O king of Judah , who sits upon the throne of David : you and your servants , and your people , who enter through these gates .
And do not be willing to sadden the new arrival , or the orphan , or the widow , nor should you burden them unfairly .
22:4 For if you will indeed accomplish this word , then there will enter through the gates of this house kings from the stock of David , sitting on his throne , and riding on chariots and on horses : they , and their servants , and their people .
22:6 For thus says the Lord about the house of the king of Judah : You are to me like Gilead , the head of Lebanon .
22:7 And I will sanctify over you the destroying man and his weapons .
22:8 And many nations will pass through this city .
Lament for him who is departing , for he will return no more , nor will he see his native land again .
22:12 Instead , he will die in the place to which I have transferred him , and he will not see this land anymore .
22:14 And he says : ‘I will build a broad house for myself , with spacious upper rooms.’ He makes windows for himself , and he builds the roof out of cedar , and he paints it with red ocher .
Did your father not eat and drink , and act with judgment and justice , so that it would be well with him ?
Was this not because he knew me , says the Lord ?
22:19 He will be buried with the burial of a donkey , having rotted and been thrown out of the gates of Jerusalem .
And utter your voice in Bashan , and cry out to those passing by .
22:21 I spoke to you in your abundance , and you said , ‘I will not listen.’ This has been your way from your youth , for you have not listened to my voice .
22:26 And I will send you , and your mother who conceived you , into a foreign land , in which you were not born , and there you shall die .
Why have they been cast out , he and his offspring , cast out even into a land that they have not known ?
Listen to the word of the Lord !
For there will not be a man from among his offspring who will sit upon the throne of David , or have authority in Judah , anymore.”
23:1 “Woe to the shepherds who scatter and tear apart the sheep of my pasture , says the Lord .
Behold , I will visit upon you because of your evil pursuits , says the Lord .
And I will return them to their own fields .
23:4 And I will raise up shepherds over them , and they will pasture them .
And no one among their number will be seeking more , says the Lord .
All my bones are trembling .
The plains of the desert have dried up , and their course has become hazardous , and their firmness has become uneven.”
For I will bring evils over them , in the year of their visitation , says the Lord .
They have prophesied in Baal , and they have deceived my people Israel .
23:16 Thus says the Lord of hosts : “Do not choose to listen to the words of the prophets who prophesy to you and deceive you .
Who has considered his word and heard it ?
23:20 The fury of the Lord will not return until it succeeds , and until it completes the plan of his heart .
23:22 If they had stood in my counsel , and if I had made my words known to my people , certainly I would have turned them away from their evil ways and from their most wicked plans .
23:25 I have heard what the prophets have said , prophesying falsehoods in my name , and also saying : ‘I have dreamed !
23:26 How long will this be in the heart of the prophets who predict what is false , and who prophesy deceptions from their own heart ?
For what has the chaff to do with the wheat , says the Lord ?
23:30 Therefore , behold : I am against the prophets , says the Lord , who steal my words , each one from his neighbor .
’ I will visit upon that man and upon his house .
And what has the Lord said ? ’
For each one’s own word will be a burden .
23:37 And then you will speak in this way to the prophet : ‘What has the Lord answered you ?
23:40 And I will give you over to an everlasting reproach and an eternal disgrace , which shall never be wiped away into oblivion.”
24:1 The Lord revealed to me , and behold , two baskets full of figs were set before the temple of the Lord , after Nebuchadnezzar , the king of Babylon , carried away Jeconiah , the son of Jehoiakim , king of Judah , and his leaders , and the craftsmen and engravers of Jerusalem , and led them into Babylon .
And I will build them up , and I will not tear them down .
For they shall return to me with their whole heart .
24:9 And I will give them over , with upheaval and affliction , to all the kingdoms of the earth : to be a disgrace , and a parable , and a proverb , and a curse in all the places to which I have cast them out .
The same is the first year of Nebuchadnezzar , the king of Babylon .
25:3 “From the thirteenth year of Josiah , the son of Amon , the king of Judah , even until this day , which is the twenty-third year , the word of the Lord has been given to me , and I have spoken to you , rising while it was still night , and speaking , and yet you have not listened .
25:6 And do not choose to go after strange gods , so that you would serve them and adore them .
And then I will not afflict you .
And I will destroy them , and I will set them in the midst of stupor and hissing , and continual desolations .
25:11 And this entire land will be in desolation and in stupor .
25:12 And when the seventy years have been completed , I will visit their iniquity upon the king of Babylon , and upon that nation , and upon the land of the Chaldeans , says the Lord .
25:13 And I will lead over that land all my words , which I have spoken against it , all that has been written in this book , everything whatsoever that Jeremiah has prophesied against all the nations .
And you shall cause all the nations , to which I will send you , to drink from it .
25:17 And I received the chalice from the hand of the Lord , and I caused all the nations , to which the Lord has sent me , to drink from it :
You will not be immune !
For the Lord is entering into judgment with the nations .
I have delivered the impious to the sword , says the Lord.”
And sprinkle yourselves with ashes , O nobles of the flock !
And you will fall like precious vessels .
25:36 There is a voice of outcry from the shepherds , and a wailing among the nobles among the flock !
For the earth has become a desolation before the face of the anger of the dove , and before the face of the fury of the Lord .
