Our current pope , Pope Benedict XVI , like every pope before him , is a direct successor of the first pope , Saint Peter , who was the first Bishop of Rome .
Among his many interactions with Jesus , Peter is remembered for his exchange with Christ on the road to Caesarea Philippi , recorded in the Gospel of Matthew ( Chapter 16).
The question of Jesus ’ identity was definitively answered for His followers by Peter with divine assistance .
“ And I tell you , you are Peter , and on this rock I will build my church , and the powers of death shall not prevail against it .
This passage provides the main Biblical proof for Peter’s primacy among the Apostles .
The Bishop of Rome ( or the Pope ) is the successor of Peter .
The name “ Peter ” comes from the Aramaic word Kepha ( or Cephas ), meaning “ Rock. ” Jesus chose to give the Apostle Simon this new name at Caesarea Philippi for symbolic reasons .
It was here that Jesus chose to proclaim His plans to build a new Church on Peter that would not succumb to the passage of time .
Jesus did not mean to imply Peter would somehow replace Him as the Rock of the Church , but that he would merely represent Him as such .
Although was a rock , yet he was not the rock ; for Christ is truly the immovable rock , but Peter on account of the rock .
Christ is the King of Heaven , and the keys belong to Him alone ( Book of Revelations , 3:7).
In Matthew 16:19, Christ the King appoints His steward , Peter , to oversee the Church , His kingdom on earth , in His absence .
Peter’s decisions on these matters , moreover , shall be confirmed in heaven .
This preventive grace is infallibility .
This is not a claim that the Pope is without sin— infallibility has nothing to do with conduct , in fact —rather it is the belief that when teaching definitively on a matter of faith and morals he will be guarded by the Holy Spirit against teaching error .
Moses ’ authority , too , was handed down through a line of successors .
Peter and the Popes fulfill a similar role in the New Covenant , serving as Christ’s earthly representative through whom God speaks to the people to resolve religious disputes and maintain unity among the faithful .
It is Peter who ends the dispute , teaching the assembly on doctrine ( see Acts of the Apostles , 15:7).
Interestingly , those who have rejected the Pope’s role have suffered doctrinal confusion and ongoing ( and accelerating ) division , which is evidenced by the explosion of non-Catholic , Christian sects .
, God ) through us ( i.e. , the Church of Rome ), let them know that they will involve themselves in transgression and in no small danger .
