Wherever the impetus of the spirit was to go , there they went .
1:13 And as for the likeness of the living creatures , their appearance was like that of burning coals of fire , and like the appearance of lamps .
1:16 And the appearance of the wheels and their work was like the appearance of the sea .
And they did not turn as they went .
And the entire body was full of eyes all around each of the four .
And when they were lifted up from the earth , the wheels , too , were lifted up together , so as to follow them .
1:22 And above the heads of the living creatures was the likeness of a firmament : similar to crystal , but dreadful to behold , and extending over their heads from above .
One of them was covered by two wings on his body , and the other was covered similarly .
When they walked , it was like the sound of a multitude , like the sound of an army .
1:25 For when a voice came from above the firmament , which was over their heads , they stood still , and they put down their wings .
And over the likeness of the throne , there was a likeness with the appearance of a man above it .
And from his waist and upward , and from his waist downward , I saw something with the appearance of fire shining all around .
This was the appearance of the splendor on every side .
2:1 This was the vision of the likeness of the glory of the Lord .
And I heard him speaking to me ,
They and their fathers have betrayed my covenant , even to this day .
And you shall say to them : ‘Thus says the Lord God.’
2:7 Therefore , you shall speak my words to them , so that perhaps they may hear and be quieted .
3:3 And he said to me : “Son of man , your stomach shall eat , and your interior shall be filled with this scroll , which I am giving to you.” And I ate it , and in my mouth it became as sweet as honey .
3:5 For you will be sent , not to a people of profound words or of an unknown language , but to the house of Israel ,
But if you were sent to them , they would listen to you .
For they are not willing to listen to me .
3:8 Behold , I have made your face stronger than their faces , and your forehead harder than their foreheads .
You should not fear them , and you should not have dread before their face . For they are a provoking house.”
3:11 And go forth and enter to those of the transmigration , to the sons of your people .
3:13 and the voice of the wings of the living creatures striking against one another , and the voice of the wheels following the living creatures , and the voice of a great commotion .
And I went forth in bitterness , with the indignation of my spirit .
3:15 And I went to those of the transmigration , to the stockpile of new crops , to those who were living beside the river Chebar .
And I remained there for seven days , while mourning in their midst .
3:18 If , when I say to the impious man , ‘You shall certainly die , ’ you do not announce it to him , and you do not speak so that he may turn aside from his impious way and live , then the same impious man will die in his iniquity .
3:19 But if you announce it to the impious man , and he is not converted from his impiety and from his impious way , then indeed he will die in his iniquity .
He shall die , because you have not announced to him .
Yet truly , I will attribute his blood to your hand .
And you will have delivered your own soul.”
And behold , the glory of the Lord was standing there , like the glory that I saw beside the river Chebar .
3:26 And I will cause your tongue to adhere to the roof of your mouth .
And you shall draw upon it the city of Jerusalem .
4:3 And you shall take up for yourself an iron frying pan , and place it as an iron wall between you and the city .
And you shall place the iniquities of the house of Israel on it by the number of days that you will sleep on it .
4:7 And you shall turn your face toward the siege of Jerusalem , and your arm shall be extended .
4:8 Behold , I have surrounded you with chains .
4:12 And you shall eat it like barley bread baked under ashes .
4:13 And the Lord said : “So shall the sons of Israel eat their bread , polluted among the Gentiles , to whom I will cast them out.”
Behold , my soul has not been polluted , and from my infancy even until now , I have not eaten anything that has died of itself , nor that which has been torn up by beasts , and no unclean flesh at all has entered into my mouth.”
4:17 So then , when bread and water fail , each one may fall against his brother .
And you shall obtain for yourself a balance for weighing , and you shall divide the hair .
And you shall take a third part , and you shall cut it with the knife all around .
5:3 And you shall take from there a small number .
5:4 And again , you shall take from them , and you shall throw them into the midst of the fire , and you shall burn them with fire .
5:6 And she has despised my judgments , so as to be more impious than the Gentiles , and my precepts , more so than the lands that are all around her .
5:9 And I will do in you what I have not done before , and the likes of which I will not do again , because of all your abominations .
And I will execute judgments in you , and I will winnow your entire remnant in every wind .
5:12 One third part of you will die by pestilence or be consumed by famine in your midst .
Yet truly , one third part of you I will scatter to every wind , and I will unsheathe the sword after them .
5:15 And you shall be a disgrace and a blasphemy , an example and an astonishment , among the Gentiles , who are all around you , when I will have executed judgments in you , in fury and in indignation and with rebukes of wrath .
At that time , I will send among them the most grievous arrows of famine , which shall bring death , and which I will send so that I may destroy you .
5:17 And I will send among you famine and very harmful beasts , even unto utter ruin .
And I will bring the sword over you .
6:2 “Son of man , set your face toward the mountains of Israel , and you shall prophesy against them ,
Thus says the Lord God to the mountains and hills and cliffs and valleys : Behold , I will lead over you the sword .
6:4 And I will demolish your altars .
And I will throw down your slain before your idols .
And I will scatter your bones around your altars .
And your altars will be broken and destroyed .
6:8 And I will leave among you those who will escape the sword among the Gentiles , when I will have dispersed you upon the earth .
’ For they will fall by the sword , by famine , and by pestilence .
But whoever is near will fall by the sword .
And I will fulfill my indignation among them .
And they shall know that I am the Lord.”
Instead , I will set your ways upon you , and your abominations will be in your midst .
7:5 Thus says the Lord God : “One affliction , behold , one affliction is approaching .
It has been vigilant against you .
7:7 Destruction is coming over you , who live upon the earth .
And you shall know that I am the Lord , who is striking .
And there shall be no rest for them .
Whoever buys should not rejoice .
For wrath is over all of their people .
For the vision concerning their entire multitude will not turn back .
And yet there is no one who may go to battle .
7:15 The sword is outside , and the pestilence and the famine are inside .
And they will be among the mountains , like doves in steep valleys , with everyone of them trembling , each one because of his iniquity .
7:19 Their silver will be thrown away , and their gold will be like a dunghill .
Because of this , I have let it be an uncleanness for them .
7:22 And I will avert my face from them , and they will violate my place of mystery .
7:24 And I will lead in the most sinful among the Gentiles , and they will possess their houses .
7:26 Disturbance will follow after disturbance , and rumor after rumor .
7:27 The king will mourn , and the prince will be clothed with grief , and the hands of the people of the earth will be greatly disturbed .
8:1 And it happened that , in the sixth year , in the sixth month , on the fifth of the month , I was sitting in my house , and the elders of Judah were sitting before me , and the hand of the Lord God fell upon me there .
From the appearance of his waist , and downward , there was fire .
And he brought me into Jerusalem , within a vision of God , next to the inner gate that looked toward the north , where there was stationed an idol of rivalry , so as to provoke an envious emulation .
8:6 And he said to me : “Son of man , you see what these ones are doing , the great abominations that the house of Israel is committing here .
And I saw , and behold , there was an opening in the wall .
8:9 And he said to me : “Enter and see the most wicked abominations which they are committing here.”
8:11 And there were seventy men out of the elders of the house of Israel , with Jaazaniah , the son of Shaphan , standing in their midst , and they stood before the pictures .
And a cloud of smoke rose up from the incense .
8:13 And he said to me : “If you turn again , you will see even greater abominations , which these ones are committing.”
And behold , at the door of the temple of the Lord , between the vestibule and the altar , there were about twenty-five men with their backs toward the temple of the Lord , and their faces toward the east .
My eye will not be lenient , nor will I take pity .
9:2 And behold , six men were approaching from the way of the upper gate , which looks to the north .
Also , one man in their midst was clothed with linen , and an instrument for writing was at his waist .
9:3 And the glory of the Lord of Israel was taken up , from the cherub upon which he was , to the threshold of the house .
9:4 And the Lord said to him : “Cross through the middle of the city , in the center of Jerusalem , and seal a Tau upon the foreheads of the grieving men , who are mourning over all the abominations which are being committed in its midst.”
But all upon whom see the Tau , you shall not kill .
9:8 And when the slaughter was completed , I remained .
Will you now destroy the entire remnant of Israel , by pouring out your fury upon Jerusalem ? ”
10:2 And he spoke to the man who was clothed with linen , and he said : “Enter , between the wheels that are under the cherubim , and fill your hand with the coals of fire that are between the cherubim , and pour them upon the city.” And he entered , in my sight .
10:5 And the sound of the wings of the cherubim was heard even in the outer court , like the voice of Almighty God speaking .
10:7 And one cherub extended his hand , from the midst of the cherubim , to the fire that was between the cherubim .
10:8 And there appeared amid the cherubim the likeness of the hand of a man , under their wings .
10:10 And in their appearance , each one of the four were similar , as if a wheel were in the midst of a wheel .
10:12 And their entire body , with their necks and their hands and their wings and the circles , were full of eyes all around the four wheels .
10:16 And when the cherubim advanced , the wheels also went beside them .
For the spirit of life was in them .
10:19 And the cherubim , lifting up their wings , were raised up from the earth in my sight .
And it stood at the entrance to the east gate of the house of the Lord .
10:20 This is the living creature , which I saw under the God of Israel beside the river Chebar .
10:22 And , concerning the appearance of their faces , these were the same faces that I had seen beside the river Chebar , and the gaze and force of each one of them was to go before his face .
11:1 And the Spirit lifted me up , and he brought me to the east gate of the house of the Lord , which looks toward the rising of the sun .
