22:3 And you shall reveal to her all her abominations .
22:4 You have offended by your blood , which you shed from yourself .
And you have caused your days to approach , and you have brought on the time of your years .
22:5 Those that are near and those that are far from you will triumph over you .
22:6 Behold , the leaders of Israel have each used his arm to shed blood within you .
The new arrival has been oppressed in your midst .
22:8 You have spurned my sanctuaries , and you have defiled my Sabbaths .
They have worked wickedness in your midst .
22:12 They have accepted bribes among you to shed blood .
And you have forgotten me , says the Lord God .
22:14 How can your heart endure , or your hands prevail , in the days that I will bring upon you ?
22:15 And I will disperse you among the nations , and I will scatter you among the lands , and I will cause your uncleanness to fade away from you .
22:19 Because of this , thus says the Lord God : Since you have all turned into dross , therefore , behold , I will gather you together in the midst of Jerusalem ,
So will I gather you together in my fury and in my wrath , and I will be quieted , and I will melt you down .
22:22 Just as silver is melted in the midst of the furnace , so will you be in its midst .
22:25 There is a conspiracy of prophets in her midst .
They have taken riches and a price .
22:26 Her priests have despised my law , and they have defiled my sanctuaries .
And they have not understood the difference between defiled and clean .
And I was profaned in their midst .
They have afflicted the needy and the poor , and they have oppressed the new arrival by accusations without judgment .
22:31 And so I poured out my indignation upon them ; in the fire of my wrath I consumed them .
In that place , their breasts were conquered ; the breasts of their adolescence were subdued .
And I held them , and they bore sons and daughters .
23:7 And she distributed her fornications to those chosen men , all of them sons of the Assyrians .
23:8 Moreover , she also did not abandon her fornications , which she had done in Egypt .
23:9 Because of this , I have delivered her into the hands of her lovers , into the hands of the sons of the Assur , whom she has lustfully desired .
23:12 She shamelessly offered herself to the sons of the Assyrians , to the rulers and magistrates who brought themselves to her clothed with colorful garments , to the horsemen who were carried by horses , and to the youths , all of them exceptional in appearance .
23:14 And she increased her fornications .
23:15 with belts wrapped around the waist , and with dyed headdresses on their heads , having seen the appearance of all the rulers , the likenesses of the sons of Babylon and of the land of the Chaldeans in which they were born ,
23:17 And when the sons of Babylon had gone to her , to the bed of breasts , they defiled her with their fornications , and she was polluted by them , and her soul was gorged by them .
And my soul withdrew from her , as my soul had withdrawn from her sister .
23:20 And she was mad with lust after lying with them , whose flesh is like the flesh of donkeys , and whose flow is like the flow of horses .
23:22 Because of this , Oholibah , thus says the Lord God : Behold , I will raise up against you all of your lovers , with whom your soul has been gorged .
23:23 the sons of Babylon , and all the Chaldeans , the nobles , the sovereigns and princes , all the sons of the Assyrians , youths of exceptional form , all the rulers and magistrates , the leaders among leaders , and the renowned riders of horses .
They will be armed against you on every side with armor and shield and helmet .
And what remains will fall by the sword .
23:26 And they will strip you of your vestments , and take away the articles of your glory .
Neither shall you lift up your eyes toward them , and you shall no longer remember Egypt .
23:29 And they will act toward you with hatred , and they will take away all your labors , and they will send you away naked and filled with disgrace .
23:32 Thus says the Lord God : You will drink the chalice of your sister , deep and wide .
23:33 You will be filled with inebriation and sorrow , by the chalice of grief and sadness , by the chalice of your sister Samaria .
For I have spoken , says the Lord God .
23:36 And the Lord spoke to me , saying : “Son of man , should you not judge Oholah and Oholibah , and announce to them their crimes ?
Moreover , they have offered even their children , whom they bore for me , to them to be devoured .
23:39 And when they immolated their children to their idols , they also entered my sanctuary on the same day , so that they defiled it .
23:40 They sent for men who were coming from far away , to whom they had sent a messenger .
23:41 You sat upon a very beautiful bed , and a table was adorned before you , on which you placed my incense and my ointment .
And concerning certain men , who were being led out of a multitude of persons , and who were arriving from the desert , they placed bracelets on their hands and beautiful crowns on their heads .
23:45 But there are just men ; these shall judge them with the judgment of adulteresses and with the judgment of those who shed blood .
23:46 For thus says the Lord God : Lead upon them a multitude , and hand them over to tumult and to pillaging .
They will put to death their sons and daughters , and they will burn their houses with fire .
And all women shall learn not to act according to their wickedness .
24:3 And you shall speak , through a proverb , a parable to the inciting house .
24:4 Pile together within it every morsel , every good piece , the thigh and the shoulder , the choice pieces and those full of bones .
Its cooking has boiled over , and its bones in its midst have been thoroughly cooked .
Cast it out piece by piece !
24:7 For her blood is in her midst ; she has shed it upon the smoothest rock .
24:8 So shall I bring my indignation over her , and take my vengeance .
24:9 Because of this , thus says the Lord God : Woe to the city of blood , out of which I will make a great funeral pyre .
So then , neither will you be cleansed before I cause my indignation over you to cease .
It shall happen , and I will act .
I will judge you according to your ways and according to your intentions , says the Lord.”
Let the band of your crown be on you , and let your shoes be on your feet .
And in the morning , I did just as he had instructed me .
Your sons and your daughters , whom you have forsaken , will fall by the sword.’
You shall not cover your faces , and you shall not eat the food of those who mourn .
And you shall know that I am the Lord God.’ ”
And you shall speak , and you shall no longer be silent .
25:3 And you shall say to the sons of Ammon : Listen to the word of the Lord God : Thus says the Lord God : Because you have said , ‘Well , well ! ’ over my sanctuary , when it was profaned , and over the land of Israel , when it was desolated , and over the house of Judah , when they were led into captivity ,
25:5 And I will make Rabbah into the habitation of camels , and the sons of Ammon into the resting place of cattle .
25:6 For thus says the Lord God : Because you have clapped your hands and stomped your foot , and have rejoiced with all your heart against the land of Israel ,
And I will destroy you from the peoples , and I will perish you from the lands , and I will crush you .
25:8 Thus says the Lord God : Because Moab and Seir have said , ‘Behold , the house of Judah is like all the Gentiles !
25:10 with the sons of Ammon , to the sons of the East , and I will give it to them as an inheritance , so that there may no longer be a remembrance of the sons of Ammon among the Gentiles .
25:13 therefore , thus says the Lord God : I will extend my hand over Idumea , and I will take from it both man and beast , and I will make it desolate from the south .
And they shall know my vengeance , says the Lord God .
25:16 because of this , thus says the Lord God : Behold , I will extend my hand over the Philistines , and I will destroy those who destroy , and I will perish the remnant of the maritime regions .
And they shall know that I am the Lord , when I will send my vengeance upon them.”
The gates of the peoples have been broken !
I will be filled .
26:3 because of this , thus says the Lord God : Behold , I am against you , O Tyre , and I will cause many nations to rise up against you , just as the waves of the sea rise up .
And I will scrape her dust from her , and I will make her into the barest rock .
26:6 Likewise , her daughters who are in the field will be slain by the sword .
26:7 For thus says the Lord God : Behold , I will lead into Tyre : Nebuchadnezzar , the king of Babylon , a king among kings , from the north , with horses , and chariots , and horsemen , and companies , and a great people .
And he will surround you with fortifications , and he will put together a rampart on all sides .
26:10 He will cover you with the inundation of his horses and with their dust .
26:13 And I will cause the multitude of your songs to cease .
For I have spoken , says the Lord God.”
26:16 And all the leaders of the sea will descend from their thrones .
They will sit on the ground , and they will wonder with astonishment at your sudden downfall .
26:19 For thus says the Lord God : When I will have made you a desolate city , like the cities that are uninhabited , and when I will have led the abyss over you , and many waters will have covered you ,
27:3 And you shall say to Tyre , which lives at the entrance to the sea , which is the marketplace of the peoples for the many islands : Thus says the Lord God : O Tyre , you have said , ‘I am of perfect beauty ,
’ Your neighbors , who built you , have filled up your beauty .
They have taken cedars from Lebanon , so that they might make a mast for you .
27:9 The elders of Gebal and its experts were considered as sailors making use of your diverse equipment .
27:10 The Persians , and the Lydians , and the Libyans were your men of war in your army .
27:11 The sons of Arwad were with your army upon your walls all around .
The many islands were the marketplace of your hand .
27:17 Judah and the land of Israel , these were your peddlers of the best grain ; they offered balsam , and honey , and oil , and resins at your festivals .
Your merchants came to you with lambs , and rams , and young goats .
27:24 These were your merchants in many places , with windings of hyacinth and of colorful weavings , and with precious treasures , which were wrapped and bound with cords .
27:25 The ships of the sea were important to your business dealings .
27:27 Your riches , and your treasures , and your versatile equipment , your sailors and your navigators , who handle your goods and who were first among your people , likewise your men of war , who were among you , and your entire multitude that is in your midst : they will fall in the heart of the sea on the day of your ruin .
27:29 And all who were handling the oar will descend from their ships ; the sailors and all the navigators of the sea will stand upon the land .
And they will cast dust upon their heads , and they will be sprinkled with ashes .
And they will weep for you with bitterness of soul , with a very bitter weeping .
’ 27:33 For by the going forth of your merchandise by sea , you supplied many peoples ; by the multitude of your riches and of your people , you enriched the kings of the earth .
27:35 All the inhabitants of the islands have been stupefied over you ; and all their kings , having been struck by the tempest , have changed their expression .
You have been reduced to nothing , and you shall not be again , even forever.”
28:3 Behold , you are wiser than Daniel ; no secret is concealed from you .
28:5 By the multitude of your wisdom , and by your business dealings , you have multiplied strength for yourself .
28:6 Therefore , thus says the Lord God : Because your heart has been exalted as if it were the heart of God ,
And you will die the death of those slain in the heart of the sea .
28:10 You will die the death of the uncircumcised at the hand of foreigners .
28:13 You were with the delights of the Paradise of God .
The work of your beauty was of gold , and your fissures were ready in the day when you were formed .
28:16 By the multitude of your business dealings , your interior was filled with iniquity , and you sinned .
28:17 And your heart was exalted by your beauty ; you have destroyed your own wisdom by your beauty .
I have presented you before the face of kings , so that they may examine you .
Therefore , I will produce a fire from your midst , which will consume you , and I will make you into ashes upon the earth , in the sight of all who are watching you .
You were made out of nothing , and you shall not be , forever.”
And they will fall , slain by the sword , on every side in her midst .
28:24 And the house of Israel will no longer be a stumbling block of bitterness , nor a thorn bringing pain everywhere around them , to those who turn against them .
28:25 Thus says the Lord God : “When I will have gathered together the house of Israel , from the peoples among whom they have been dispersed , I shall be sanctified in them in the sight of the Gentiles .
29:2 “Son of man , set your face against Pharaoh , the king of Egypt , and you shall prophesy about him and about all of Egypt .
I have given you to the beasts of the earth and to the birds of the air , to be devoured .
For you have been a staff made of reed to the house of Israel .
And when they leaned on you , you shattered , and so you injured all of their lower backs .
29:9 And the land of Egypt will be a desert and a wilderness .
And I will make the land of Egypt into a wilderness , destroyed by the sword from the tower of Syene all the way to the borders of Ethiopia .
And they will be desolate for forty years .
29:13 For thus says the Lord God : After the end of forty years , I will gather the Egyptians from the peoples among whom they had been scattered .
And in that place , they will be a lowly kingdom .
And they shall know that I am the Lord God.”
And wages have not been paid to him , nor to his army , for Tyre , for the service by which he served for me against it .
And he will take its multitude , and he will prey upon its profits , and he will plunder its spoils .
29:21 In that day , a horn will spring forth for the house of Israel , and I will give to you an open mouth in their midst .
And there will be dread in Ethiopia , when the wounded will have fallen in Egypt , and its multitude will have been taken away , and its foundations will have been destroyed .
30:6 Thus says the Lord God : And those who prop up Egypt will fall , and the arrogance of its reign will be brought down .
30:7 And they will be scattered into the midst of desolate lands , and its cities will be in the midst of cities that have been deserted .
30:9 In that day , messengers will go forth from my face in Greek warships , in order to crush the confidence of Ethiopia .
30:10 Thus says the Lord God : By the hand of Nebuchadnezzar , the king of Babylon , I will cause the multitude of Egypt to cease .
And they will draw their swords over Egypt .
And by the hands of foreigners , I will utterly destroy the land and its plenitude .
30:13 Thus says the Lord God : And I will destroy the graven images , and I will cause the idols of Memphis to cease .
And I will send terror upon the land of Egypt .
30:15 And I will pour out my indignation upon Pelusium , the strength of Egypt , and I will kill the multitude of Alexandria .
Pelusium will be in pain , like a woman giving birth .
Then her daughters will be led into captivity .
30:22 Because of this , thus says the Lord God : Behold , I am against Pharaoh , the king of Egypt , and I will shatter his strong arm , which has already been broken .
30:23 And I will disperse Egypt among the nations , and I will scatter them among the lands .
And I will put my sword into his hand .
And the arms of Pharaoh will fall .
30:26 And I will disperse Egypt among the nations , and I will scatter them among the lands .
Its rivers have flowed around his roots , and it has sent forth its streams to all the trees of the regions .
31:6 And when he had extended his shadow , all the birds of the air made their nests in his branches , and all the beasts of the forest conceived their young under his foliage , and an assembly of the many peoples lived under his shadow .
For his root was near many waters .
The spruce trees were not equal to his summit , and the plane trees were not equal to his fullness .
31:9 For I made him beautiful , and dense with many branches .
31:10 Because of this , thus says the Lord God : Since he was sublime in height , and he made his summit green and dense , and his heart was exalted because of his height ,
And all the peoples of the earth will withdraw from his shadow , and abandon him .
31:14 For this reason , none of the trees among the waters will exalt themselves because of their height , nor will they place their summits above the thick branches and foliage , nor will any of those that are irrigated stand out because of their height .
And I held back its rivers , and I restrained the many waters .
31:16 I shook the Gentiles with the sound of his ruin , when I led him down to hell , with those who were descending into the pit .
31:18 To whom can you be compared , O famous and sublime one , among the trees of pleasure ?
You will sleep in the midst of the uncircumcised , with those who have been slain by the sword .
32:2 “Son of man , take up a lamentation over Pharaoh , the king of Egypt , and you shall say to him : You are like the lion of the Gentiles , and like the dragon that is in the sea .
32:3 Because of this , thus says the Lord God : I will spread my net over you , with the multitude of many peoples , and I will draw you into my dragnet .
I will cast you upon the surface of the field .
And I will satiate the beasts of the entire earth with you .
And I will fill up your hills with your decaying flesh .
And the valleys will be filled with you .
32:8 I will cause all the lights of heaven to grieve over you .
32:9 And I will provoke the heart of many peoples to anger , when I will have led in your destruction among the Gentiles , over the lands that you have not known .
And their kings will be afraid , with great horror , over you , when my sword will begin to fly above their faces .
All these nations are invincible , and they will lay waste to the arrogance of Egypt , and so its multitude will be destroyed .
32:15 when I will have set the land of Egypt in desolation .
They have dragged her down , with all her people .
32:23 Their graves have been placed in the lowest parts of the pit .
32:24 Elam is in that place , with all his multitude , on all sides of his grave , all those who were slain or who fell by the sword , who descended uncircumcised to the lowest part of the earth , who caused their terror in the land of the living .
32:25 They have appointed him a place to lie among all his people , in the midst of the slain .
All these are uncircumcised and were slain by the sword .
They have been stationed in the midst of the slain .
Their graves are all around him : all these are uncircumcised , and they were slain and fell by the sword .
32:28 Therefore , you also will be broken in the midst of the uncircumcised , and you will sleep with those who were slain by the sword .
And they have borne their disgrace , with those who descend into the pit .
32:32 For I have spread my terror in the land of the living , and he has gone to sleep in the midst of the uncircumcised , with those who were slain by the sword , even Pharaoh and all his multitude , says the Lord God.”
33:3 and if he sees the sword approaching over the land , and he sounds the trumpet , and he announces to the people ,
33:5 He heard the sound of the trumpet , and he did not take care of himself , so his blood will be upon him .
33:9 But if you have announced to the impious man , so that he may be converted from his ways , and he has not converted from his way , then he will die in his iniquity .
33:11 Say to them : As I live , says the Lord God , I do not desire the death of the impious , but that the impious should convert from his way and live .
For why should you die , O house of Israel ?
33:13 Even now , if I say to the just man that he shall certainly live , and so , with confidence in his justice , he commits iniquity , all his justices will be delivered into oblivion , and by his iniquity , which he has done , by this he shall die .
33:15 and if that impious man returns the collateral , and repays what he has taken by force , and if he walks in the commandments of life , and does not do anything unjust , then he shall certainly live , and he shall not die .
He has done judgment and justice , so he shall certainly live .
33:18 For when the just man will have withdraw from his justice , and committed iniquities , he shall die by these .
33:22 But the hand of the Lord had been upon me in the evening , before the one who had fled arrived .
And since my mouth had been opened , I was no longer silent .
33:24 “Son of man , as for those who live in these ruinous ways on the soil of Israel , when speaking , they say : ‘Abraham was one man , and he possessed the land as an inheritance .
33:30 And as for you , O son of man : the sons of your people speak about you beside the walls and in the doorways of houses .
Should not the flocks be fed by the shepherds ?
But my flock you did not feed .
What was broken , you have not bound , and what was cast aside , you have not led back again , and what was lost , you have not sought .
34:5 And my sheep were scattered , because there was no shepherd .
34:6 My sheep have wandered to every mountain and to every exalted hill .
And there was no one who sought them ; there was no one , I say , who sought them .
34:8 As I live , says the Lord God , since my flocks have become a prey , and my sheep have been devoured by all the wild beasts of the field , since there was no shepherd , for my shepherds did not seek my flock , but instead the shepherds fed themselves , and they did not feed my flocks :
Neither will the shepherds feed themselves any more .
And I will deliver them from all the places to which they had been scattered in the day of gloom and darkness .
And I will pasture them on the mountains of Israel , by the rivers , and in all the settlements of the land .
There they will rest on the green grass , and they will be fed in the fat pastures , on the mountains of Israel .
And I will bind up what had been broken .
For you even trample with your feet upon the remainder of your pastures .
34:19 And my sheep were pastured from what you had trampled with your feet , and they drank from what your feet had disturbed .
34:21 For you have pushed with your sides and shoulders , and you have threatened all the weak cattle with your horns , until they were scattered abroad .
34:23 And I will raise up over them ONE SHEPHERD , who will feed them , my servant David .
And I will cause the very harmful beasts to cease from the land .
34:27 And the tree of the field will yield its fruit , and the land will yield its crop .
Instead , they will live in confidence without any terror .
And they will be no longer be diminished by famine in the land , nor will they carry any longer the reproach of the Gentiles .
35:5 For you have been a continual adversary , and you have enclosed the sons of Israel , by the hands of the sword , in the time of their affliction , in the time of extreme iniquity .
Even though you have hated blood , blood will pursue you .
And I will take away from it the one who departs and the one who returns .
In your hills , and in your valleys , as well as in your torrents , the slain will fall by the sword .
35:11 Because of this , as I live , says the Lord God , I will act in accord with your own wrath , and in accord with your own zeal , by which you have acted with hatred toward them .
35:12 And you shall know that I , the Lord , have heard all your disgraces , which you have spoken about the mountains of Israel , saying : ‘They are deserted .
35:14 Thus says the Lord God : When the whole earth will rejoice , I will reduce you to solitude .
You will be laid waste , O mount Seir , with all of Idumea .
36:3 because of this , prophesy and say : Thus says the Lord God : Because you have been made desolate , and you have been trampled on every side , and you have been made into an inheritance for the remainder of the nations , and because you rose up , over the tip of the tongue and over the shame of the people ,
Thus says the Lord God to the mountains , and to the hills , to the torrents , and to the valleys , and to the deserts , and to the ruins , and to the forsaken cities , which have been depopulated and ridiculed by the remainder of the nations all around :
36:6 Therefore , prophesy over the soil of Israel , and you shall say to the mountains , and to the hills , to the ridges , and to the valleys : Thus says the Lord God : Behold , I have spoken in my zeal and in my fury , because you have endured the shame of the Gentiles .
36:8 But as for you , O mountains of Israel , spring forth your branches , and bear your fruit , to my people Israel .
And the cities shall be inhabited , and the ruinous places shall be restored .
36:13 Thus says the Lord God : Because they are saying about you , ‘You are a woman who devours men , and you are strangling your own nation , ’
36:15 Neither will I permit men to discover in you the shame of the Gentiles any more .
I have judged them according to their ways and their plans .
36:21 But I have spared my holy name , which the house of Israel has defiled among the Gentiles , to whom they entered .
36:23 And I will sanctify my great name , which was defiled among the Gentiles , which you have defiled in their midst .
36:24 Certainly , I will take you away from the Gentiles , and I will gather you together from all the lands , and I will lead you into your own land .
36:30 And I will multiply the fruit of the tree and the produce of the field , so that you may no longer bear the disgrace of famine among the nations .
And you will be displeased by your own iniquities and your own crimes .
36:34 and when the deserted land will have been cultivated , which previously was desolate to the eyes of all who passed by ,
36:36 And the Gentiles , those who remain around you , shall know that I , the Lord , have built up what was destroyed , and have planted what was uncultivated .
36:38 like a holy flock , like the flock of Jerusalem in her solemnities .
37:1 The hand of the Lord was set upon me , and he led me away in the Spirit of the Lord , and he released me in the midst of a plain which was full of bones .
Now they were very many upon the face of the plain , and they were exceedingly dry .
And you shall say to them : Dry bones , listen to the word of the Lord !
37:6 And I will set sinews upon you , and I will cause flesh to grow over you , and I will extend skin over you .
But a noise occurred , as I was prophesying , and behold : a commotion .
37:8 And I saw , and behold : sinews and flesh rose up over them ; and skin was extended over them .
They say : ‘Our bones are dried out , and our hope has perished , and we have been cut off.’
And I will lead you into the land of Israel .
And you shall know that I , the Lord , have spoken and acted , says the Lord God.”
37:16 “And as for you , son of man , take up a piece of wood for yourself , and write upon it : ‘For Judah , and for the sons of Israel , his companions.’ And take up another piece of wood , and write upon it : ‘For Joseph , the wood of Ephraim , and for the entire house of Israel , and for his companions.’
And they will be united in your hand .
37:19 you shall say to them : Thus says the Lord God : Behold , I will take up the wood of Joseph , which is in the hand of Ephraim , and the tribes of Israel , which are joined to him , and I will put them together with the wood of Judah , and I will make them one piece of wood .
37:22 And I will make them one nation in the land , on the mountains of Israel , and one king will be ruler over all .
And they will be my people , and I will be their God .
They shall walk in my judgments , and they shall keep my commandments , and they shall do them .
And they shall live upon it , they and their sons , and the sons of their sons , even for all time .
And I will establish them , and multiply them .
37:28 And the Gentiles shall know that I am the Lord , the Sanctifier of Israel , when my sanctuary will be in their midst , forever.”
And I will lead you away , with all your army , the horses and the horsemen all clothed in armor , a great multitude , equipped with spears and light shields and swords ,
38:6 Gomer , and all his companies , the house of Togarmah , the northern parts , and all his strength , and the many peoples with you .
At the end of the years , you will arrive at the land which was turned back by the sword , and which has been gathered from many peoples to the mountains of Israel that have been continually abandoned .
38:9 But you will ascend and arrive like a tempest and like a cloud , so that you may cover the land , you and all your companies , and the many peoples with you .
All these live without a wall ; they have no bars or gates.’
38:13 Sheba , and Dedan , and the merchants of Tarshish , and all its lions will say to you : ‘Could you have arrived in order to purchase from the spoils ?
And I will lead you over my own land , so that the Gentiles may know me , when I will have been sanctified in you , O Gog , before their eyes .
38:18 And this shall be in that day , in the day of the advent of Gog over the land of Israel , says the Lord God : my indignation will rise up in my fury .
38:20 And before my face there shall be stirred up : the fish of the sea , and the flying things of the air , and the beasts of the field , and every crawling thing that moves across the soil , and all the men who are upon the face of the earth .
38:21 And I will call for the sword against him on all my mountains , says the Lord God .
38:22 And I will judge him by pestilence , and blood , and violent rainstorms , and immense hailstones .
And I will bring you over the mountains of Israel .
39:4 You will fall upon the mountains of Israel , you and all your companies , and your peoples who are with you .
39:6 And I will send a fire upon Magog , and upon those who are living confidently in the islands .
39:7 And I will make known my holy name in the midst of my people , Israel , and my holy name will no longer be defiled .
39:9 And the inhabitants from the cities of Israel will go forth , and they will kindle and burn the weapons , the shields and the spears , the bows and the arrows , and the staff and the lance .
39:10 And they will not carry wood from the countryside , and they will not cut from the forests .
And they will prey upon those who had preyed upon them , and they will plunder those who had plundered them , says the Lord God .
And in that place , they will bury Gog and all his multitude , and it will be called the valley of the multitude of Gog .
39:13 Then all the people of the earth will bury them , and this shall be for them a renown day , on which I have been glorified , says the Lord God .
Then , after seven months , they will begin to seek .
And when they will have seen the bone of a man , they will station a marker beside it , until the undertakers may bury it in the valley of the multitude of Gog .
Rush together from every side to my victim , which I have immolated for you , a great victim upon the mountains of Israel , so that you may consume flesh , and drink blood !
39:19 And you shall consume the fat unto satiation , and you shall drink the blood unto inebriation , from the victim that I will immolate for you .
39:22 And the house of Israel shall know that I am the Lord , their God , from that day and thereafter .
And so I concealed my face from them , and I delivered them into the hands of their enemies , and they all fell by the sword .
39:25 Because of this , thus says the Lord God : Now I will lead back the captivity of Jacob , and I will take pity upon the entire house of Israel .
39:28 And they shall know that I am the Lord , their God , because I carried them away to the nations , and I gathered them upon their own land , and I did not abandon any of them there .
