4:5 And you will be ruined on this day , and now the prophet will be ruined with you .
4:6 My people have become silent because they had no knowledge .
4:7 According to the multitude of them , so have they sinned against me .
4:8 They will devour the sins of my people , and they will lift up their souls towards their iniquity .
Since they have abandoned the Lord , they will not be safeguarded .
4:12 My people have inquired of their stave , and their staff has announced to them .
4:13 They have offered sacrifice on the tops of the mountains and burnt incense on the hills , under the oak , and the poplar , and the terebinth tree , because its shadow was good ; therefore , your daughters will commit fornication and your spouses will be adulteresses .
4:15 If you commit fornication , Israel , at least let Judah not commit offenses ; and do not be willing to enter into Gilgal , nor to ascend to Bethaven , and neither should you swear , “As the Lord lives.”
4:17 Ephraim participates in idolatry , so send him away .
They love to bring disgrace to their protectors .
5:3 I know Ephraim , and Israel has not been hidden from me , yet now Ephraim has committed fornication , and Israel has been contaminated .
5:5 And the arrogance of Israel will answer to his face .
5:6 With their flocks and their herds , they will go to seek the Lord , and they will not find him .
5:7 They have sinned against the Lord .
Now one month will devour them with all their own .
5:10 The leaders of Judah have become like those who assume the end .
5:11 Ephraim has been enduring malicious slander and broken judgment , because he began to go after filth .
5:13 And Ephraim saw his own weakness , and Judah his chains .
But he will not be able to heal you , nor is he able to release you from your chains .
I myself will seize and go forth .
5:15 I will go and return to my place , until you shall grow faint and seek my face .
6:1 In their tribulation , they will arise early to me .
6:3 He will revive us after two days ; on the third day he will raise us up , and we will live in his sight .
