Who has measured the height of heaven, and the breadth of the earth, and the depth of the abyss?
1:6 To whom has the root of wisdom been revealed, and who has recognized her astuteness?
And who has understood the multiplicity of her steps?
1:9 He created wisdom through the Holy Spirit, and he saw her, and numbered her, and measured her.
1:11 The fear of the Lord is glory, and honor, and rejoicing, and a crown of exultation.
1:13 It will be well, in the very end, for him who fears the Lord, and on the day that he passes away, he will be blessed.
1:19 It will be well with him who fears the Lord, and at the consummation of his days, he will be blessed.
But to sinners, wisdom is an abomination.
1:28 For he who is without fear is not able to be justified.
1:35 And what pleases him is faith and meekness.
1:36 You should not be incredulous to the fear of the Lord.
1:37 You should not be a hypocrite in the sight of men.
2:1 Son, when you apply yourself to the service of God, stand in justice and in fear, and prepare your soul for temptation.
2:3 Endure steadfastly for God.
2:6 Believe God, and he will restore you to health.
Observe his fear, and grow old in it.
And your reward will not be taken away.
And mercy will approach you, to your delight.
2:12 For who has remained in his commandment and been abandoned?
2:13 For God is upright and merciful, and he will forgive sins in the day of tribulation. And he is the Protector to all those who seek him in truth.
2:15 Woe to the dissolute in heart, who do not trust God!
2:19 Those who fear the Lord will seek the things that are well-pleasing to him.
2:20 Those who fear the Lord will prepare their hearts, and they will sanctify their souls in his sight.
2:22 saying: “If we do not do penance, then we will fall into the hands of the Lord, and not into the hands of men.”
3:4 He who loves God will plead with him on behalf of sins, and will keep himself away from sin, and will be heeded in the prayers of his days.
3:16 For even in return for the sin of the mother, good will be repaid to you.
3:22 You should not seek the things that are too high for you, and you should not examine the things that are beyond your ability.
But you should not be curious in too many of his works.
3:30 The synagogue of the arrogant will not be healed.
He remembers him afterwards, and in the time of his fall, he will find a firm support.
4:5 You should not avert your eyes from the needy out of anger.
4:6 For the pleadings of him who speaks curses of you, in the bitterness of his soul, will be heeded.
4:11 And then you shall be like an obedient son of the Most High, and he will take pity on you more than a mother would.
4:14 Those who hold to her will inherit life.
4:15 Those who serve her will yield to what is holy.
4:16 He who listens to her shall judge the nations.
You should not conceal your wisdom in her beauty.
And understanding and knowledge and doctrine are discerned in the words of those who understand and by their steadfastness in the works of justice.
For these things will not benefit you in the day of darkness and retribution.
5:13 Be meek when listening to a word, so that you may understand.
5:14 If you understand, then answer your neighbor.
6:7 If you would obtain a friend, test him before you accept him, and do not trust him readily.
6:9 And there is a friend who can be turned to animosity.
6:12 If he humbles himself before you and hides himself from your face, you shall have a noble and harmonious friendship.
6:23 For the wisdom of doctrine is in accord with her name, and she is not manifest to many.
And if you adapt your mind, you will be wise.
And if you love to listen, you will be wise.
And he himself will give a heart to you, and the desire of wisdom will be given to you.
7:1 Do not choose to do evil, and evil will not take hold of you.
7:6 Do not seek to become a judge, unless you have sufficient strength to shatter iniquities.
7:7 You should not sin against the multitude of a city, nor should you cast yourself against the people.
For even in one sin, you will not go unpunished.
7:12 You should not ridicule a man in bitterness of soul.
For the practice of lying is not good.
7:19 Humble your spirit greatly.
For the grace of her modesty is above gold.
7:23 Let an understanding servant be loved by you like your own soul.
And if they are useful, let them remain with you.
Watch over their bodies.
And you should not forget the complaints of your mother.
And so, give back to them as they also have done for you.
7:34 Give them their portion, just as it has been commanded of you, from the first-fruits and from the purifications.
7:35 You should offer to the Lord the gift of your strength, and the sacrifice of sanctification, and the first-fruits of what is holy.
7:39 Do not let yourself be slow to visit the sick.
8:3 For gold and silver have destroyed many, and have reached and corrupted even the hearts of kings.
Remember that we are all subject to correction.
8:15 You should not lend to a man who is stronger than you.
8:16 You should not promise beyond your ability.
8:17 You should not judge against a judge.
8:18 You should not go forth on the way with an audacious man, lest perhaps he may burden you with his evils.
8:19 You should not start a conflict with an angry man, and you should not go into the desert with an audacious man.
8:20 You should not hold counsel with the foolish.
8:21 You should not take counsel in the sight of an outsider.
9:1 You should not be jealous of the wife of your bosom, lest she reveal, because of you, the malice of a wicked lesson.
9:5 You should not stare at a virgin, lest perhaps you may be scandalized by her beauty.
9:11 Many, by admiring the beauty of the wife of another, have become reprobate.
9:12 You should not sit down at all with another man’s wife, nor recline with her on a couch.
9:14 You should not abandon a old friend.
9:16 You should not envy the glory and wealth of a sinner.
For you would be entering the midst of snares, and walking upon the arms of the grieving.
