12:3 As for you , then , son of man , prepare for yourself the supplies for traveling far away , and travel away in the daytime in their sight .
Then you shall go forth in the evening in their presence , just as one goes forth who is moving far away .
And you shall go out through it .
You shall cover your face , and you shall not see the ground .
And in the evening , I dug myself through the wall by hand .
12:10 Say to them : Thus says the Lord God : This is the burden concerning my leader who is in Jerusalem , and concerning the entire house of Israel , who are in their midst .
Just as I have done , so shall it be done to them .
12:12 And the leader who is in their midst will be carried on shoulders ; he will go forth in darkness .
His face will be covered , so that he may not see the land with his eye .
And I will lead him to Babylon , into the land of the Chaldeans , but he himself will not see it .
12:14 And all who are around him , his guards and his companies , I will scatter into every wind .
12:15 And they shall know that I am the Lord , when I will have dispersed them among the Gentiles , and will have sowed them among the lands .
12:19 And say to the people of the land : Thus says the Lord God , to those who are living in Jerusalem , in the land of Israel : They shall eat their bread in anxiety , and drink their water in desolation , so that the land may be desolate before its multitude , because of the iniquity of all who are living in it .
12:23 Therefore , say to them : Thus says the Lord God : I will cause this proverb to cease , and it shall no longer be a common saying in Israel .
12:24 For there shall be no longer be any empty visions , nor any ambiguous divination in the midst of the sons of Israel .
And whatever word I will speak , it shall be done , and it shall not be delayed any more .
13:2 “Son of man , prophesy to the prophets of Israel who are prophesying , and you shall say to those who prophesy from their own heart : Hear the word of the Lord :
13:6 They see emptiness , and they foretell falsehoods , saying , ‘The Lord says , ’ though the Lord has not sent them .
13:7 Have you not seen a futile vision and spoken a lying divination ?
13:8 Because of this , thus says the Lord God : Since you have spoken emptiness and have seen falsehoods , therefore : behold , I am against you , says the Lord God .
They shall not be in the council of my people , and they shall not be written in the writing of the house of Israel .
And they have built a wall , but they have covered it in clay without straw .
And I will level it to the ground , and its foundation will be revealed .
13:16 the prophets of Israel , who prophesy to Jerusalem , and who see visions of peace for her when there is no peace , says the Lord God .
And when they have seized the souls of my people , they became the life of their souls .
13:20 Because of this , thus says the Lord God : Behold , I am against your little pillows , with which you catch flying souls .
And I will release the souls that you are capturing , the souls that should fly .
And I will free my people from your hand .
And I will rescue my people from your hand .
So why should I respond when they inquire of me ?
14:5 so that the house of Israel may be seized within their own heart , by which they have withdrawn from me to all their idols .
14:7 For the man , the man of the house of Israel , and the new arrival among the converts who may be in Israel , if he is alienated from me , and he sets his idols in his heart , and he stations the scandal of his iniquity before his face , and he approaches the prophet , so that he may inquire of me through him : I , the Lord , will respond to him through myself .
And I will perish him from the midst of my people .
14:9 And when a prophet has gone astray and has spoken a word : I , the Lord , have deceived that prophet .
14:11 So may the house of Israel no longer go astray from me , nor be polluted by all their transgressions .
And I will send a famine upon it , and I will destroy from it both man and beast .
14:15 And if I also lead in very harmful beasts upon the land , so that I devastate it , and it becomes impassable , so that no one may cross through it because of the beasts ,
But only they themselves will be delivered , for the land shall be desolated .
14:18 and if these three men were in its midst , as I live , says the Lord God , they will deliver neither sons , nor daughters , but only they themselves will be delivered .
14:20 and if Noah , and Daniel , and Job were in its midst , as I live , says the Lord God , they will deliver neither son , nor daughter , but they will deliver only their own souls by their justice .
14:22 yet still there shall be left within it some who will be saved , who shall lead away their own sons and daughters .
And you shall be consoled concerning the evil that I have brought upon Jerusalem , concerning all the things that I have brought to bear upon it .
15:3 Can any wood be taken from it , so that it may be made into a work , or formed into a peg so as to hang some kind of vessel upon it ?
The fire consumes both its ends ; and its middle is reduced to ashes .
15:6 Therefore , thus says the Lord God : Like the stalk of the vine among the trees of the forests , which I have given to be devoured by fire , so will I deliver the inhabitants of Jerusalem .
15:8 and when I will have made their land impassable and desolate .
16:2 “Son of man , make known to Jerusalem her abominations .
16:4 And when you were born , on the day of your nativity , your umbilical cord was not cut , and you were not washed with water for health , nor salted with salt , nor wrapped with cloths .
Instead , you were cast upon the face of the earth , in the abjection of your soul , on the day when you were born .
And you were multiplied and became great , and you advanced and arrived at the ornament of a woman .
And behold , your time was the time of lovers .
And I swore to you , and I entered into a covenant with you , says the Lord God , and you became mine .
16:11 I adorned you with ornaments , and I put bracelets upon your hands and a necklace around your neck .
16:13 And you were adorned with gold and silver , and you were clothed in fine linen , woven with many colors .
And you became very beautiful .
16:14 And your renown went forth among the Gentiles , because of your beauty .
16:16 And taking from your garments , you made for yourself exalted things , having sewed together disparate pieces .
16:17 And you took your beautiful items , made of my gold and my silver , which I gave to you , and you made for yourself images of men , and you fornicated with them .
And you placed my oil and my incense before them .
And so it was done , says the Lord God .
Is your fornication a small matter ?
16:22 And after all your abominations and fornications , you have not remembered the days of your youth , when you were naked and full of shame , wallowing in your own blood .
16:24 you built for yourself a brothel , and you made for yourself a place of prostitution in every street .
And you caused your beauty to become abominable .
And I will give you to the souls of those who hate you , the daughters of the Philistines , who are ashamed of your wicked way .
And even then , you were not satisfied .
16:31 For you have built your brothel at the head of every way , and you have made your exalted place on every street .
16:32 but instead like a woman who is an adulteress , who prefers strangers to her own husband .
For in as much as you have given payment , and not taken payment , what has been done in you is the contrary.”
16:36 Thus says the Lord God : “Because your money has been poured out , and your disgrace has been uncovered , in your fornications with your lovers and with the idols of your abominations , in the blood of your sons , whom you gave to them :
And I will gather them together against you on every side .
16:38 And I will judge you with the judgment of adulteresses and of those who shed blood .
And they will strip you of your vestments .
And they will leave you behind , naked and full of disgrace .
And they will stone you with stones , and massacre you with their swords .
16:43 For you have not remembered the days of your youth , and you have provoked me in all these things .
16:44 Behold , all who speak a common proverb will take this up against you , saying : ‘Like the mother , so also is her daughter.’
And you are the sister of your sisters , for they cast away their husbands and their children .
16:46 And your older sister is Samaria , she and her daughters are those who live to your left .
You have acted almost more wickedly , in all your ways , than they have acted .
16:49 Behold , this was the iniquity of Sodom , your sister : arrogance , indulgence in bread and abundance , and the idleness of her and her daughters ; and they did not reach out their hand to the needy and the poor .
And so I took them away , just as you have seen .
For you have exceeded them in your wickedness , and you have justified your sisters by all your abominations , which you have wrought .
So they have been justified above you .
16:53 But I will convert and restore them , by converting Sodom with her daughters , and by converting Samaria and her daughters .
16:54 So may you bear your disgrace and be confounded over all that you have done , consoling them .
And Samaria and her daughters will return to their ancient state .
16:58 You have borne your wickedness and your disgrace , says the Lord God.”
16:60 And I will remember my covenant with you in the days of your youth .
16:61 And you shall remember your ways and be confounded , when you will have received your sisters , your elder with your younger .
And he took the kernel of the cedar .
17:5 And he took from the seed of the land and placed it in the ground for seed , so that it might take firm root above many waters ; he placed it at the surface .
And its roots were underneath it .
17:7 And there was another large eagle , with great wings and many feathers .
17:8 It had been planted in a good land , above many waters , so that it would produce branches and bear fruit , so that it would become a large vine .
Should he not pull up its roots , and strip off its fruit , and dry up all the branches that it has produced , and let it wither , though he is without a strong arm and without many people to pull it up by the root ?
What if it does not prosper ?
Say : Behold , the king of Babylon arrives in Jerusalem .
17:13 And he will take one from the offspring of the king , and he will strike a pact with him and receive an oath from him .
17:14 so that it may be a lowly kingdom , and may not lift itself up , and may instead keep his pact and serve it .
Should he who has done these things prosper and obtain safety ?
17:16 As I live , says the Lord God , in the place of the king , who appointed him as king , whose oath he has made void , and whose pact he has broken , under which he was living with him , in the midst of Babylon , he shall die .
And so , since he has done all these things , he shall not escape .
17:21 And all his fugitives , with all his procession , will fall by the sword .
And you shall know that I , the Lord , have spoken.”
I will tear off a tender twig from the top of its branches , and I will plant it on a mountain , lofty and exalted .
17:24 And all the trees of the regions will know that I , the Lord , have brought low the sublime tree , and have exalted the lowly tree , and have dried up the green tree , and have caused the dry tree to flourish .
18:2 “Why is it that you circulate among yourselves this parable , as a proverb in the land of Israel , saying : ‘The fathers ate a bitter grape , and the teeth of the sons have been affected.’
The soul that sins , the same shall die .
18:6 and if he does not eat upon the mountains , nor lifted up his eyes to the idols of the house of Israel , and if he has not violated the wife of his neighbor , nor approached a menstruating woman ,
18:8 if he has not lent upon usury , nor taken any increase , if he has averted his hand from iniquity , and has executed true judgment between man and man ,
18:12 who grieves the needy and the poor , who seizes with violence , who does not restore the collateral , and who lifts up his eyes to idols , committing abomination ,
His blood shall be upon him .
18:15 who does not eat upon the mountains , nor lift up his eyes to the idols of the house of Israel , and who does not violate the wife of his neighbor ,
18:17 who has averted his hand from injuring the poor , who has not taken usury and an overabundance , who has acted according to my judgments and walked in my precepts , then this one shall not die for the iniquity of his father ; instead , he shall certainly live .
18:22 I will not remember all his iniquities , which he has worked ; by his justice , which he has worked , he shall live .
18:24 But if a just man turns himself away from his justice , and does iniquity in accord with all the abominations that the impious man so often does , why should he live ?
How could it be that my way is not fair ?
18:26 For when the just man turns himself away from his justice , and commits iniquity , he shall die by this ; by the injustice that he has worked , he shall die .
18:28 For by considering and turning himself away from all his iniquities , which he has worked , he shall certainly live , and he shall not die .
And then why should you die , O house of Israel ?
So return and live.”
19:4 And the Gentiles heard about him , and they seized him , but not without receiving wounds .
19:5 Then , when she had seen that she was weakened , and that her hope had perished , she took one of her little ones , and appointed him as a lion .
And he learned to seize prey and to devour men .
And the land , with its plenitude , was made desolate by the voice of his roaring .
19:10 Your mother is like a vine , in your blood , planted by the water ; her fruit and her branches have increased because of many waters .
And she saw her own loftiness among the multitude of her branches .
19:14 And a fire has gone forth from a rod of her branches , which has consumed her fruit .
This is a lamentation , and it shall be a lamentation.”
20:1 And it happened that , in the seventh year , in the fifth month , on the tenth of the month , men from the elders of Israel arrived , so that they might inquire of the Lord , and they sat before me .
20:3 “Son of man , speak to the elders of Israel , and you shall say to them : Thus says the Lord God : Have you arrived in order to inquire of me ?
20:4 If you judge them , if you judge , O son of man , reveal to them the abominations of their fathers .
20:6 in that day , I lifted up my hand for their sake , so that I would lead them away from the land of Egypt , into a land which I had provided for them , flowing with milk and honey , which was singular among all lands .
I am the Lord your God.’
20:9 But I acted for the sake of my name , so that it would not be violated in the sight of the Gentiles , in the midst of whom they were , and among whom I appeared to them , so that I might lead them away from the land of Egypt .
20:13 But the house of Israel provoked me in the desert .
20:14 But I acted for the sake of my name , lest it be violated before the Gentiles , from whom I cast them out , in their sight .
20:16 For they cast aside my judgments , and they did not walk in my precepts , and they violated my Sabbaths .
20:17 Yet my eye was lenient concerning them , so that I did not utterly destroy them , nor did I consume them in the desert .
And do not be defiled by their idols .
Walk in my precepts , and observe my judgments , and accomplish them .
And so , I threatened that I would pour out my fury upon them , and that I would fulfill my wrath among them in the desert .
20:23 Again , I lifted up my hand against them , in the wilderness , so that I would disperse them among the nations , and scatter them among the lands .
20:26 And I defiled them by their own gifts , when they offered everything that opened the womb , because of their offenses .
20:28 though I had led them into the land , about which I lifted up my hand , so that I might give it to them : They saw every lofty hill and every leafy tree , and there they immolated their victims , and there they presented the provocation of their oblations , and there they stationed their sweet fragrances , and poured out their libations .
20:31 And you are being defiled by all of your idols , even to this day , by the oblation of your gifts , when you lead your sons through the fire .
20:33 As I live , says the Lord God , I will reign over you with a strong hand , and with an outstretched arm , and with fury poured forth .
And I will gather you from the lands into which you were dispersed .
20:35 And I will lead you into the desert of the peoples , and there I will enter into judgment with you , face to face .
20:37 And I will subject you to my scepter , and I will lead you into the bonds of the covenant .
And I will lead them away from the land of their sojourn , but they shall not enter into the land of Israel .
20:40 on my holy mountain , on the exalted mountain of Israel , says the Lord God , there all the house of Israel shall serve me ; all of them , I say , in the land in which they shall please me , and there I will require your first-fruits , and the foremost of your tithes , with all your sanctifications .
And I will be sanctified in you before the eyes of the nations .
20:43 And there you shall remember your ways and all your wickedness , by which you have been defiled .
20:46 “Son of man , set your face against the way of the south , and pour in drops toward Africa , and prophesy against the forest of the field of the meridian .
And every face will be burned up within it , from the south , even to the north .
21:2 “Son of man , set your face toward Jerusalem , and pour in drops toward the sanctuaries , and prophesy against the soil of Israel .
21:4 But in as much as I have slain among you the just and the impious , for this reason my sword will go forth from its sheath against all flesh , from the south even to the north .
21:6 And as for you , son of man , groan in the breaking of your back , and groan in bitterness before them .
’ you shall say : ‘On behalf of the report , For it is approaching .
The sword has been sharpened and polished !
It has been polished , so that it may shine !
You have cut down every tree .
This sword has been sharpened , and it has been polished , so that it may be in the hand of the one who kills .
For this has been done among my people , this is among all the leaders of Israel , who have fled .
This is the sword of the great slaughter , which causes them to be utterly stupefied ,
At all their gates , I have presented the consternation of the sword , which has been sharpened and polished so as to shine , which has been dressed for the slaughter .
Go to the right or to the left , whichever way is the desire of your face .
21:21 For the king of Babylon stood at the fork , at the head of the two ways , seeking divination , shuffling arrows ; he inquired of idols , and he consulted entrails .
21:32 You will be food for the fire ; your blood will be in the midst of the land ; you will be delivered to oblivion .
And you have been defiled by your idols which you yourself made .
Because of this , I have made you a disgrace to the Gentiles , and a derision to all the lands .
You are filthy , infamous , great in destruction .
22:7 They have abused father and mother within you .
They have grieved the orphan and the widow among you .
22:9 Maligning men were within you , in order to shed blood , and they have eaten upon the mountains within you .
22:10 They have uncovered the nakedness of their father within you .
22:11 And each one has committed abomination with the wife of his neighbor .
The brother has oppressed his sister , the daughter of his father , within you .
All these are brass , and tin , and iron , and lead in the midst of the furnace ; they have become like the dross of silver .
22:21 And I will gather you together , and I will burn you in the fire of my fury , and you will be melted in its midst .
And you shall know that I am the Lord , when I will have poured out my indignation upon you.”
And they have averted their eyes from my Sabbaths .
22:27 Her leaders in her midst are like wolves seizing the prey : to shed blood , and to perish souls , and to continually pursue profit with avarice .
22:29 The people of the land have oppressed with slander and have seized with violence .
22:30 And I sought among them for a man who might set up a hedge , and stand in the gap before me on behalf of the land , so that I might not destroy it ; and I found no one .
I have rendered their own way upon their head , says the Lord God.”
As for their names : Oholah is Samaria , and Oholibah is Jerusalem .
23:6 who were clothed with hyacinth : rulers and magistrates , passionate youths and all of the horsemen , mounted on horses .
And she defiled herself with the uncleanness of all those whom she madly desired .
23:10 They uncovered her shame ; they took away her sons and daughters ; and they slew her with the sword .
And they carried out judgments in her .
And her fornication was beyond the fornication of her sister .
And when she had seen men depicted on the wall , the images of the Chaldeans , expressed in colors ,
23:16 she became mad for them with the desire of her eyes , and she sent messengers to them in Chaldea .
23:18 Also , her fornications were uncovered , and her shame was revealed .
23:21 And you have revisited the crimes of your youth , when your breasts were conquered in Egypt , and the breasts of your adolescence were subdued .
And I will gather them together against you all around :
23:24 And they will overwhelm you , well-equipped with chariot and wheel , a multitude of peoples .
And I will give judgment to their eyes , and they will judge you with their judgments .
They will cut off your nose and your ears .
They will seize your sons and your daughters , and your youngest will be devoured by fire .
23:27 And I will cause your wickedness to cease from you , and your fornication to cease from the land of Egypt .
23:28 For thus says the Lord God : Behold , I will deliver you into the hands of those whom you have hated , into the hands by which your soul has been gorged .
And the shame of your fornication will be revealed : your crimes and your fornications .
23:31 You have walked in the way of your sister , and so I will give her chalice into your hand .
You will be held in derision and in ridicule , to a very great extent .
23:37 For they are adulteresses , and blood is in their hands , and they have fornicated with their idols .
23:38 But they have done even this to me : They have defiled my sanctuary on the same day , and they have profaned my Sabbaths .
They have done these things , even in the midst of my house .
And so , behold , they arrived , those for whom you washed yourself , and smeared cosmetics around your eyes , and were adorned with feminine ornaments .
23:42 And the voice of a multitude was exulting within her .
23:43 And I said about her , as she was being worn away by her adulteries , ‘Even now , she continues in her fornication ! ’
For they are adulteresses , and blood is on their hands .
23:47 And may they be stoned with the stones of the peoples , and may they be pierced with their own swords .
24:2 “Son of man , write for yourself the name of this day , on which the king of Babylon was confirmed against Jerusalem today .
24:5 Take the fattest from the flock , and arrange also a heap of bones under it .
24:6 Because of this , thus says the Lord God : Woe to the city of blood , to the cooking pot that has rust in it , and whose rust has not gone out of it !
No lot has fallen upon it .
She has not shed it upon the ground , so that it could be covered with dust .
I have presented her blood upon the smoothest rock , so that it would not be covered .
24:12 There has been much sweat and labor , and yet its extensive rust has not gone out of it , not even by fire .
For I wanted to cleanse you , and you have not been cleansed from your filth .
24:17 Groan silently ; you shall make no mourning for the dead .
And my wife died in the evening .
24:21 ‘Speak to the house of Israel : Thus says the Lord God : Behold , I will defile my sanctuary , the pride of your realm , and the desire of your eyes , and the dread of your soul .
In accord with all that he has done , so shall you do , when this will happen .
24:25 “And as for you , son of man , behold , in the day when I will take away from them their strength , and the joy of their dignity , and the desire of their eyes , in which their souls find rest : their sons and their daughters ,
25:2 “Son of man , set your face against the sons of Ammon , and you shall prophesy about them .
25:4 therefore , I will deliver you to the sons of the East , as an inheritance .
25:7 therefore , behold , I will extend my hand over you , and I will deliver you as a spoil of the Gentiles .
25:12 Thus says the Lord God : Because Idumea has taken vengeance , so as to vindicate herself against the sons of Judah , and has sinned grievously , and has sought revenge against them ,
And those who are in Dedan will fall by the sword .
And they shall act in Idumea in accord with my wrath and my fury .
25:15 Thus says the Lord God : Because the Philistines have taken vengeance , and have revenged themselves with all their soul , destroying , and fulfilling ancient hostilities ,
25:17 And I will execute great vengeance against them , reproving them in fury .
She has been turned toward me .
She will be deserted ! ’
26:4 And they will break apart the walls of Tyre , and they will destroy its towers .
26:5 She will be a drying place for nets from the midst of the sea .
26:8 Your daughters who are in the field , he will kill with the sword .
And he will lift up a shield against you . 26:9 And he will combine moveable shelters and battering rams before your walls , and he will destroy your towers with his armaments .
He will cut down your people with the sword , and your noble statues will fall to the ground .
They will despoil your businesses .
And the sound of your stringed instruments will no longer be heard .
And you will no longer be built up .
26:15 Thus says the Lord God to Tyre : “Will not the islands shake at the sound of your ruin and at the groans of your slain , when they will have been cut down in your midst ?
And they will cast aside their outer garments and their colorful clothing , and they will be clothed in stupor .
26:17 And taking up a lamentation over you , they will say to you : ‘How could you have perished , you who live in the sea , the famous city that was strong in the sea , with your inhabitants , of whom the whole world was in dread ? ’
And the islands of the sea will be disturbed , because no one goes out from you .
26:20 and when I will have dragged you down with those who descend into the pit to the everlasting people , and when I will have assembled you in the lowest parts of the earth , like the desolate places of antiquity , with those who have been brought down into the pit , so that you will be uninhabited , and moreover , when I will have given glory to the land of the living :
27:4 for I have been positioned at the heart of the sea !
27:5 They constructed you with spruce from Senir , with all the planks of the sea .
27:6 They have formed your oars from the oaks of Bashan .
27:7 Colorful fine linen from Egypt was woven for you as a sail to be placed upon the mast ; hyacinth and purple from the islands of Elishah were made into your covering .
Your wise ones , O Tyre , were your navigators .
All the ships of the sea and their sailors were your merchants among the people .
And even the Gammadim , who were in your towers , suspended their quivers on your walls on all sides ; they completed your beauty .
27:13 Greece , Tubal , and Meshech , these were your peddlers ; they traveled to your people with slaves and with brass vessels .
They traded teeth of ivory and of ebony for your price .
Because of the multitude of your works , they offered jewels , and purple , and patterned cloth , and fine linen , and silk , and other valuables in your market .
27:18 The Damascene was your trader in the multitude of your works , in greatly diverse wealth , in rich wine , in wool with the finest coloring .
Storax ointment and sweet flag were in your marketplace .
27:21 Arabia and all the leaders of Kedar , these were the merchants at your hand .
27:22 The vendors of Sheba and Raamah , these were your merchants , with all the finest aromatics , and precious stones , and gold , which they offered in your marketplace .
For you were replenished and exceedingly glorified in the heart of the sea .
The south wind has worn you down in the heart of the sea .
27:30 And they will howl over you with a great voice , and they will cry out with bitterness .
27:32 And they will take up a mournful verse over you , and they will lament you : ‘What city is like Tyre , which has become mute in the midst of the sea ?
27:34 Now you have been worn away by the sea , your opulence is in the depths of the waters , and your entire multitude that was in your midst has fallen .
28:4 By your wisdom and prudence , you have made yourself strong , and you have acquired gold and silver for your storehouses .
And your heart has been exalted by your strength .
28:7 for this reason , behold , I will lead over you foreigners , the most robust among the Gentiles .
28:12 and you shall say to him : Thus says the Lord God : You were the seal of similitudes , full of wisdom and perfect in beauty .
28:14 You were a cherub , stretched out and protecting , and I stationed you on the holy mountain of God .
And I cast you away from the mountain of God , and I perished you , O protecting cherub , from the midst of the stones containing fire .
I have cast you to the ground .
28:18 You have defiled your sanctuaries , by the multitude of your iniquities and by the iniquity of your business dealings .
28:23 And I will send a pestilence upon her , and there will be blood in her streets .
And they shall build houses and plant vineyards .
And they shall know that I am the Lord their God.”
And I will draw you out of the midst of your rivers , and all your fish will adhere to your scales .
You will fall upon the surface of the earth ; you will not be taken up , nor gathered together .
29:6 And all the inhabitants of Egypt shall know that I am the Lord .
29:7 When they took hold of you with the hand , you broke , and so you wounded all of their shoulders .
29:8 Because of this , thus says the Lord God : Behold , I will lead the sword over you , and I will destroy both man and beast from among you .
29:12 And I will set the land of Egypt in desolation , in the midst of desolate lands , and its cities in the midst of overturned cites .
And I will scatter the Egyptians among the nations , and I will disperse them among the lands .
29:14 And I will lead back the captivity of Egypt , and I will collect them in the land of Pathros , in the land of their nativity .
29:15 It will be the lowest among the other kingdoms , and it will no longer be exalted above the nations .
29:16 And they will no longer be the confidence of the house of Israel , teaching iniquity , so that they may flee and follow them .
Every head was shaven , and every shoulder was stripped of hair .
29:19 Because of this , thus says the Lord God : Behold , I will station Nebuchadnezzar , the king of Babylon , in the land of Egypt .
